=== TARGET 3 DEFAULT PROTOCOL CLARIFICATION ===

Spec states: 'Default transport protocol for new RPC configurations should be
             transport.Framed instead of transport.PurePayload (0)'

This means: When creating a new client/server WITHOUT specifying a protocol,
            it should default to Framed, not PurePayload

Looking for where this default is set in initialization code:

1. rpcconfig.initialize() method:
func (r *rpcConfig) initialize() {
	r.readOnlyMask = 0
	r.rpcTimeout = defaultRPCTimeout
	r.connectTimeout = defaultConnectTimeout
	r.readWriteTimeout = defaultReadWriteTimeout
	r.ioBufferSize = defaultBufferSize
	r.transportProtocol = 0
	r.interactionMode = defaultInteractionMode
}

// Recycle reuses the rpcConfig.
--
	r.initialize()
	rpcConfigPool.Put(r)
}

